          "rte_40": "When v1 == INT_MIN (-2147483648) and v2 == -1, the Euclidean quotient is 2147483648 which exceeds INT_MAX (2147483647) and cannot be represented as int. The code computes tmp_6 = stb__div(2147483647, 1) = 2147483647, then q = tmp_6 + 1 = 2147483648 overflows. The mathematical Euclidean quotient for this input pair is inherently unrepresentable in a 32-bit signed integer."
